----- stdout -----
markdown-style — markdown hygiene: trailing spaces, tabs, blank runs, final newline
Status: fixable

What it checks
  Markdown hygiene from a curated rumdl slice: trailing spaces, hard tabs, multiple blank lines, a single final newline, and opt-in paragraph reflow. Each message is prefixed with the originating rumdl rule id.

Config [markdown-style]
  reflow (default: false) — normalize each paragraph to one line (rumdl MD013); off because it rewrites prose

Example finding
  [MD009] Trailing whitespace

Fix
  `ailint check --fix` rewrites each file in place: strips trailing spaces, converts hard tabs, collapses blank-line runs, and ensures a single final newline (and reflows paragraphs when reflow = true).

